course: dictionary
lesson: 4582
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Look at the words around them to find the right one. The word helping can mean a portion of food, it can mean giving help, and it can be part of a phrase.
explain: «Can I have a second helping of pudding, please?» Here a helping is an amount of food served to one person at one time. The clue is pudding, which you eat. Try the swap: "a second amount of food" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Helping others is kind.» Here helping means giving help, and the clue is kind. Now look at «He gave me a helping hand with my bike.» A helping hand is a phrase that means some help.
explain: Help, helps, helped and helping are all forms of the same verb. When you meet a new meaning, ask: what would fit in this sentence? Then check your meaning by putting it in place of the hard word.
fact: A helping can be a noun: one portion of food served to one person.
fact: Helping can also be a verb form: help, helps, helped, helping.
fact: «A helping hand» means some help.
fact: In Chinese, «bié kèqi» (BYEH KUH-chee) literally means «don't be polite», and it means make yourself at home.
fact: When someone invites you to take a helping, you can take one, but not the whole plate.
exercise: What does «a second helping» mean in «Can I have a second helping of pudding?» | A second time you help someone | *An amount of food served to one person at one time | A long walk to the shop
exercise: «Helping others is kind.» What does helping mean here? | *Giving help | Serving food on a plate | Going out to play
exercise: What does «a helping hand» mean? | Two hands held together for a game | *Some help | A hand that is very big
test: In the sentence «She is helping her little brother with his reading», which form of help is used? | helped | help | *helping
test: What does the Chinese invitation «bié kèqi» literally mean? | *Don't be polite | Be polite at all times | Please eat everything on the table
exam: Which meaning fits in «He gave the dog a helping of food»? | Giving help to someone | Painting a wall or a fence | *An amount of food served at one time
